 },
 "summary": "A shrouded single-row header with contacts on a 1.00 mm pitch, lying flat on the board so the mating plug enters parallel to it. The contacts are gull-wing surface-mount leads, and a solder tab at each end of the housing holds it down. The family runs from 2 to 20 circuits and then 22, 24 and 26; the 1.0-4PWB has four. Each contact is rated 50 V AC/DC and 1.0 A with AWG#28 or AWG#30 wire (0.8 A with AWG#32), from -25 to 85 °C.",
